  "description": "SUTSOR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C106 H121 La6 N5 O39,4.39(C2 H3 N1),2.12(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 8 O neighbors; La3 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La4 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La5 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La6 (La) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.948-5.389 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.24-168.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [La6(CO3)2(naphthsao)4.5(naphthsaoH)0.5(acac)8(CO3)0.5(CH3OH)2.76H5.5(H2O)1.24]·2.39CH3CN·0.12H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
